          "Build authentic Latino community partnership beyond voter contact — at 26.83% of the district, the Latino community is large enough that proportional representation in resource allocation, hiring, and legislative focus is both a governance obligation and an electoral necessity in a district this diverse.",
          "Translate the district's $114,035 median income into tangible constituent services and economic policy that benefit renters, service workers, and younger adults — affluence on paper does not equal security for all residents, and a 69% result suggests room for deeper engagement with economic mobility and cost-of-living concerns.",
          "Monitor Latino voter engagement in primary and general cycles with specific attention to turnout, candidate preference, and issue salience — California's Latino electorate has demonstrated responsiveness to targeted messaging on immigration, community safety, and economic opportunity, and this community's baseline support should not be assumed."
