          "Engage Latino and Asian communities through concrete economic policy, not symbolic recognition—these are growing populations whose stakes in wage policy, workplace rights, education quality, and business opportunity are material and deserve specific legislative attention rather than coalition management language.",
          "Recognize that consolidation at 64% leaves 36% opposition, and evaluate whether that opposition reflects genuine policy disagreement (on taxes, regulation, housing development) or insufficient constituent service—in a district this affluent and educated, opposition voters are ideologically coherent, not persuadable, and the focus should be on maximizing turnout among the aligned base."
