          { name: "Ignoring White & Black Minority Communities", tag: "avoid", why: "At 20.45% white and 8.4% Black, these communities together represent less than 30% of CA-HD-20 but remain meaningful constituencies whose specific economic and social concerns can become invisible in a district where the political narrative centers on the Asian American and Hispanic majorities. White residents in Silicon Valley often include highly educated, high-income professionals and small business owners with distinct concerns around regulatory burden and tax policy; Black residents face persistent workforce equity and healthcare access challenges. Treating either group as automatically aligned with the broader Democratic coalition, rather than as constituencies with distinct constituent needs and potential dissatisfaction points, means governing less than four-fifths of the district with active engagement." }
