          "Engage the 34.59% Asian American constituency on specific economic mobility issues: small business access to capital and licensing, STEM education funding, professional workforce equity, and healthcare access are the material concerns for a highly educated community; treat this as an active constituent relationship requiring ongoing legislative attention, not inherited Democratic support.",
          "Build active relationship with the 30.5% Hispanic community on workforce and economic security: wage enforcement, agricultural worker protections, healthcare access, and housing affordability are the tangible issues animating this constituency; maintain regular constituent service infrastructure and demonstrate legislative progress on these concrete concerns rather than rhetorical alignment.",
          "Recognize the 73% is not a safe floor but a current result earned through alignment on economic mobility: the diverse composition of the district, the high cost of living, and the large renter population mean dissatisfaction on housing, healthcare, or workforce issues can consolidate quickly; any incumbent must demonstrate ongoing problem-solving, not assume the margin will persist absent active engagement."
