          "Engage the Asian American plurality with specificity on community priorities: education quality, immigration policy implementation (including enforcement fairness and pathway issues), small-business regulation, and public safety are issues where Asian American voters' preferences may differ from broader Democratic positioning — assuming monolithic support risks leaving persuadable voters available to a credible challenger.",
          "Build explicit governance competence messaging around service delivery and cost control: a district this educated and affluent evaluates on whether government is actually solving problems efficiently, not on abstract ideology — focus on concrete results on housing, transit, education, and public safety rather than broader partisan framing."
