          "Build a specific workforce and education pipeline narrative for young adults and families: the 34-year median age and 18.6% college attainment signal a constituency evaluating on whether their kids have real pathways to economic mobility; vocational training, community college investment, and employer partnerships are more salient than abstract education rhetoric.",
          "Consolidate the Latino coalition by addressing the distinct concerns of different cohorts within it: immigrant families may prioritize different issues than second-generation families; working renters have different stakes than homeowners; young adults face different economic pressures than aging parents—a 66% winner who expands to 70%+ must speak to these distinctions with specificity."
