          "Recognize that Anglo voter consolidation at 59% depends on maintaining Hispanic support sufficient to offset any Democratic gain among white college-educated voters—do not assume either group is locked in. The college attainment rate of 27.5% (below state median in many contexts) may include white professional voters who could be swing-persuadable on education funding or climate issues; Hispanic homeowners require affirmative economic messaging, not passive assumption.",
