          "Engage the college-educated constituency (48.5%) on student debt sustainability, professional opportunity pathways, and whether state government is removing regulatory and financial barriers to economic mobility or reinforcing them—this is a constituency that evaluates on whether their credentials translate into stable, dignified economic life.",
          "Build genuine crossethnic constituent relationships across the Hispanic (33.47%), white (29.43%), Black (21.27%), and Asian (10.28%) communities through specific policy attention to each group's economic and social priorities rather than treating the district as a monolithic progressive bloc—no single demographic commands this district, and none will be taken for granted.",
          "Treat the 19% opposition as a signal worth understanding, not dismissing—in an 81-19 district, the minority is concentrated enough that understanding whether it represents affluent renters frustrated by progressive taxation, conservative homeowners, or a specific demographic group creates opportunities for issue-specific persuasion or better targeted messaging."
