          "Build Latino constituency organization as a ground operation: the 62.57% Latino plurality is not monolithic — it includes both long-established immigrant families and newer arrivals, homeowners and renters, agricultural-connected and service-sector workers. Authentic community engagement through trusted messengers in Spanish-language media, church networks, and labor organizations reaches persuadable voters far more effectively than broadcast advertising.",
          "Offer specific economic answers for the 34.4-year median age cohort: childcare costs, healthcare affordability, wage growth, and whether young families can afford to stay in the district. This constituency is not ideologically rigid; it responds to whether government is delivering material improvement in household economic security.",
