          { name: "Treating Hispanic and Asian Communities as Subconstituencies Requiring Separate Mobilization", tag: "avoid", why: "At 51.07% combined, Hispanic and Asian residents are the demographic co-majority of CA-HD-59, yet treating them as discrete identity-based constituencies to be mobilized separately rather than as integrated professional homeowners and renters fractures the cross-ethnic consensus that generated the 61% result. The incumbent's strength lies in serving these communities as part of the broader professional and homeowner coalition, not in ethnic-specific outreach that can appear patronizing or that signals divergent interests. A challenger who attempts to mobilize Hispanic or Asian voters as separate blocs is likely to find that material interest in schools, housing, and fiscal governance outweighs ethnic-based appeals." }
