          "Engage Hispanic and Asian communities as demographic co-majorities with specific constituent attention: at 51.07% combined, these communities are the district's demographic majority, yet the consolidated 61% result suggests they are being served as part of the professional homeowner constituency rather than as distinct communities. Ensure constituent-service responsiveness, language access, and community-specific outreach (business development for entrepreneurs, skilled-worker immigration facilitation, educational pathway support for first-generation professionals) to prevent defection.",
          "Address the renter minority's housing and economic security concerns explicitly: at 29.5% renters in a $131,286-income district, the renter constituency is younger professionals and service-sector workers cost-locked into rental housing despite regional wealth. Housing affordability, tenant protections, and economic opportunity for those building wealth rather than preserving it are issues where the incumbent's record matters — and where a challenger can activate opposition if Chen appears aligned only with homeowner interests.",
