          "Defend on governance competence and service delivery effectiveness, not ideological positioning: this is a 66.7% college-educated, $126K+ income constituency that evaluates on whether government is working, not on abstract progressive values—any incumbent or challenger who leads with ideology rather than specific evidence of effective policy will lose persuadable voters in this district.",
          "Engage the 40% opposition directly and specifically: one in two voters chose the Republican alternative in 2024, and the 60-40 result is not a mandate but a contested plurality; understanding what specific governance failures or policy disagreements generated that 40% opposition is essential to defending or defeating the incumbent.",
