          { name: "Generic Party Messaging and Partisan Mobilization as Primary Strategy", tag: "avoid", why: "A 50.3% college-educated, affluent, demographically diverse constituency in a high-cost urban area does not respond reliably to generic Democratic or Republican messaging — this is an information-rich electorate that evaluates candidates on policy specificity, governance competence, and whether they demonstrate understanding of the district's actual material challenges. Any candidate who relies primarily on partisan activation rather than detailed policy analysis and demonstration of local problem-solving capacity will underperform in a district where swing voters are educated, informed, and evaluating on performance rather than inherited party loyalty." }
