          "Engage immigrant economic integration with fluency — Hispanic (27.23%) and Asian (22.47%) residents comprise half the district, and their economic advancement depends on wage theft prosecution, credential recognition pathways, and ESL access; demonstrating concrete progress on these issues is non-negotiable credibility with this coalition.",
