          "Build specific engagement with the Hispanic and Latino community around economic mobility and healthcare access: at 34.93% of the district, this population is the second-largest demographic group and the source of the opposition's current 31%; meaningful inroads require targeted conversation about wage policy, bilingual education quality, and immigrant community concerns, not generic diversity rhetoric.",
          "Do not assume Asian American voters are a Republican lock: at 8.5% of the district, this community has specific concerns about small business access to capital, immigration policy, and educational equity that deserve direct engagement rather than symbolic inclusion in coalition messaging.",
