          "Lead on economic mobility for non-college-credential pathways: at 23.2% college attainment despite $86,606 median income, the district's prosperity rests on trades, small business, and skilled service work — vocational training, apprenticeship expansion, and professional-wage job access are concrete policy anchors that resonate with this specific constituency.",
          "Engage the Hispanic majority with specificity on economic concerns, not assumed partisan loyalty: 63.4% Hispanic voters in a 59-42 district means Hispanic voters are not monolithic — address small-business support, labor market access, housing affordability, and neighborhood public safety as direct constituent concerns rather than assuming ethnic identity predicts electoral behavior.",
          "Treat housing affordability as a priority despite above-median income: the 42.1% renter rate in a $86,606-income district signals that San Diego County's cost-of-living pressures are real for this constituency and represent a legitimate policy priority, not a special-interest concern — candidates who address this directly will outperform those who treat income level as sufficient evidence of security."
